  "version": 1,
  "description": "Cross-language test vectors for Scholium record ids. Each vector carries a full record envelope; the record id is the CIDv1 (dag-cbor codec, sha2-256, base32) over the DAG-CBOR encoding of the envelope fields v, type, author, created, prev, body, proofs — excluding id and sig. dag_cbor_hex is the exact canonical DAG-CBOR byte string that gets hashed. Every implementation of the record core must produce both values from the envelope alone. The id and sig members inside the envelopes are illustrative and take no part in the computation.",
